   "text": "Thermal conductors"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Good and bad thermal conductors"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Good thermal conductors are solids which easily transfer heat\n\n  - For example; a metal pan or a ceramic tea cup\n  - Almost all metals are good thermal conductors\n- Bad thermal conductors (also called insulators) are solids which do not transfer heat well\n\n  - For example; a wool blanket or layers of cardboard or paper\n  - Non-metals or organic materials (from plants or animals) are often poor thermal conductors"
  }
 ]
